### ===================================================


### Auth Controller - /api/v1/auth


### ===================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api/v1


### ---------------------------------------------------


### Login - Valid credentials


### ---------------------------------------------------

POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@lab.local",
  "password": "Password123!"
}


### ---------------------------------------------------


### Login - Technician credentials


### ---------------------------------------------------

POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "technician@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}


### ---------------------------------------------------


### Login - Invalid email format (should fail validation)


### ---------------------------------------------------

POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "password123"
}


### ---------------------------------------------------


### Login - Missing email (should fail validation)


### ---------------------------------------------------

POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "password": "password123"
}


### ---------------------------------------------------


### Login - Missing password (should fail validation)


### ---------------------------------------------------

POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@example.com"
}


### ---------------------------------------------------


### Login - Empty body (should fail validation)


### ---------------------------------------------------

POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{}


### ---------------------------------------------------


### Login - Wrong password (should fail auth)


### ---------------------------------------------------

POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "wrongpassword"
}


### ---------------------------------------------------


### Login - Non-existent user (should fail auth)


### ---------------------------------------------------

POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nonexistent@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}
